{"id":"forest-of-argonne","name":"Forest of Argonne","qid":"Q649125","country":"France","locality":"Grand Est","lat":"49.15","lon":"4.966666666","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Natural formations","period":"","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"","type":"mountain range; natural region of France","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_of_Argonne","text":"The Forest of Argonne (French pronunciation: [aʁɡɔn] ) is a long strip of mountainous and wild woodland in northeastern France, approximately 200 km (120 mi) east of Paris. The forest measures roughly 65 km (40 mi) long and 15 km (9 mi) wide filled with many small hills and deep valleys formed by water run-off from the Aire and Aisne rivers rarely exceeding more than 200 m (650 ft) in elevation. Following the First World War, the landscape of the forest was forever changed as trench warfare led to parts of the forest being riddled with deep human-made trenches along with craters from explosives.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_of_Argonne","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-2b3b91c50603","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"ChatelChéhéryFrance.JPG","o":"gh-2b3b91c50603.jpg","credit":{"text":"Wilson44691","license":"Public domain","license_url":"","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChatelCh%C3%A9h%C3%A9ryFrance.JPG","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"battlefield-1--anders-schei-andersschei","game":"battlefield-1","name":"Anders-schei-andersschei","verified":false,"text":"","text_source":"","text_license":"","images":[{"id":"gh-p055f55a8167","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-p055f55a8167.jpg","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Battlefield 1, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://battlefield.fandom.com/wiki/File:Anders-schei-andersschei-07.jpg","via":"Fandom (battlefield)","note":"Fandom upload by 550684 on 2017-05-21"}},{"id":"gh-p4821f37a3f5","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-p4821f37a3f5.jpg","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Battlefield 1, © El